---
description: Never write AI-sounding text (em dashes, AI-tell phrases) in any user-facing copy
alwaysApply: true
---

# Write like a human, not like an AI

Every string a real person actually reads has to read like a person wrote it.
This covers: JSX/rendered text, toasts and error messages, generated
narrative copy (fun facts, investor briefing, Compound year stories, weekly
recaps, community facts), legal pages, onboarding copy, and Margus's own
generated output (chat replies, Forecast rationale, Thesis Pulse verdicts,
Upside Portfolio reports).

It does not cover code comments, TypeScript identifiers, or JSON/schema
field names the model must emit (`thesisStatus`, `convictionKey`).
Instructional prose sent *to* the model should already use grandma English
so the model does not learn the banned words as its working vocabulary.
The standard `—` placeholder for a missing/N-A table cell is also exempt.

## Never use em dashes in user-facing prose

Rewrite with a period, comma, or colon instead, whatever reads most
naturally for that sentence. This is the single biggest AI tell.

```
BAD:  "Modeled prices, not a target — Margus reasons this per ticker."
GOOD: "Modeled prices, not a target. Margus reasons this per ticker."
```

## Skip AI-tell phrases and structures

Avoid: "it's important to note," "it's important to remember," "in summary,"
"whether you're X or Y," "in today's fast-paced market,"
"unlock/leverage/elevate/dive into/harness/navigating," "delve," "testament,"
"groundbreaking," "not just X, but Y," "seamless/robust/cutting-edge," ending
every message with a tidy summary paragraph, or excessive symmetrical
rule-of-three lists.

Short, plain, slightly opinionated sentences beat balanced, hedge-everything
ones.

## No market slang

A 12-year-old and a 75-year-old should get every sentence. Never use
trader words in anything a person reads: sleeve, marks, live marks, tape,
conviction, digestion, dry powder, beta, risk-on, risk-off,
liquidity, drawdown, rotation, cadence, print (for a number), candles,
OTM, NAV, alpha, moat, TAM, capex.

Thesis is allowed. Use it for why someone owns a name (Thesis intact,
Thesis watch, Thesis broken).

Say the plain thing: group of similar stocks, today's prices, why you own
it, how sure you are, a quiet year, cash sitting ready, a jumpy name,
people buying, people selling, a drop, money moving from one group to
another.

This includes Margus output. Ban the words in `MARGUS_PERSONA` and scrub
leftovers in `humanizeMargusText`. Do not tell the model to "talk in
sleeves."

## Where this is already enforced

`MARGUS_PERSONA` in `src/lib/ai/margus-persona.ts` carries a hard Voice ban
(no em dashes, no AI-brochure cadence, speak like a PM Slack note). That is
not enough on its own: models still emit dashes. Every Margus surface also
runs generated strings through `humanizeMargusText` /
`humanizeMargusTree` in `src/lib/ai/humanize-copy.ts` before save/display
(Forecast plan API + localStorage, Thesis Pulse API + cache, Upside Portfolio
cron writes, chat markdown). Do not remove the persona ban or the sanitizer.
When adding a new generated-copy string or AI surface, write it dash-free
from the start and pipe it through the sanitizer on the way out.
